# Tasks

The source of truth for work in this project. Add new rows for new tasks; update Status and Owner as work moves.

| ID    | Title                            | Status      | Priority | Owner | Notes |
|-------|----------------------------------|-------------|----------|-------|-------|
| T-001 | Example: define the first task   | {{STATUS_READY}}       | P1       |       | Replace this row with a real task |

## Status values

| Value | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `backlog` | Known but not yet ready to work — needs scoping or prerequisites |
| `{{STATUS_READY}}` | Fully specified; safe to claim |
| `{{STATUS_IN_PROGRESS}}` | Claimed by an owner; actively worked |
| `{{STATUS_IN_REVIEW}}` | In PR / awaiting review |
| `{{STATUS_DONE}}` | Landed |

## Priority values

| Value | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `P0` | Must ship next; everything else paused |
| `P1` | Soon — current cycle |
| `P2` | When convenient |
| `P3` | Backlog; revisit when planning the next cycle |

## Adding a task

Add a new row to the table. Fill in:

- **ID** — short unique identifier (e.g. `T-042`). Pick the next number after the highest existing id.
- **Title** — one-line summary; readable in isolation
- **Status** — start at `backlog` if it needs more scoping, `{{STATUS_READY}}` if it's actionable
- **Priority** — best guess; can be revised
- **Owner** — leave blank until claimed; the `claim` skill will set this
- **Notes** — link to a design doc, related issue, or a one-line "why" / "how"

## Workflow

| Action | What to do |
|---|---|
| Claim a task | Run the `claim` skill (auto-picks the highest-priority `{{STATUS_READY}}` row) or `/claim <id>` |
| Open a PR | Update Status to `{{STATUS_IN_REVIEW}}` |
| PR merges | Update Status to `{{STATUS_DONE}}` |
| Pause work mid-task | Update Notes with where you left off; leave Status at `{{STATUS_IN_PROGRESS}}` |
| Abandon a task | Update Status to `backlog` and Owner to empty; add a Notes line explaining why |

Keep the Notes column terse — it's a pointer, not a journal. Long context belongs in linked docs.
